;; clj-kondo does not know that test.check's `defspec` defines a var, so every
;; property test read as an unresolved symbol. Teaching the linter is the fix;
;; suppressing the rule would have hidden real unresolved symbols too.
;;
;; The security hooks are this project's own, shipped in clj-kondo/ for other
;; projects to copy. They are referenced here rather than copied in: a copy
;; under .clj-kondo/ would be a second source of truth, and the copy that was
;; here before was gitignored -- so a fresh clone had a config naming a hook
;; namespace that did not exist, and clj-kondo errored on every run. CI found
;; that on its first execution.
{:lint-as {clojure.test.check.clojure-test/defspec clojure.core/def}
 :config-paths ["../clj-kondo"]}
